/-!
# The period lattice of a regular Lagrangian torus fibration

Let `σ` be a symplectic form on a boundaryless manifold `M` and let `π : M → B` be a regular
Lagrangian torus fibration (`TauCeti.SmoothTwoForm.IsNondegenerate.IsLagrangianTorusFibration`)
onto a Hausdorff manifold `B` of dimension `n`. This file constructs the action of the cotangent
space `T*_b B` on the fibre `π⁻¹(b)` and its stabilizer, the **period lattice** `Λ_b ⊆ T*_b B`.

Covectors at `b` are the elements of `F →L[ℝ] ℝ`, the dual of the model space `F = T_b B`. A
covector `α ∈ T*_b B` acts on the fibre over `b` by the time-one map of the Hamiltonian flow of
`g ∘ π`, for any `C²` function `g` on `B` with `dg_b = α`
(`IsLagrangianTorusFibration.fiberAction`,
`IsLagrangianTorusFibration.coe_fiberAction_eq_flowOf`). This does not depend on the choice of
`g`: the Hamiltonian vector field of `g ∘ π` is vertical, and along the fibre over `b` it is
determined by `d(g ∘ π) = dg_b ∘ dπ`
(`IsLagrangianFibration.flowOf_hamiltonianVectorField_comp_eq`).
The flows of pulled-back functions commute, since the fibres are Lagrangian, so this is an action of
the vector group `T*_b B` (`IsLagrangianTorusFibration.fiberAction_add`), and it is transitive
(`IsLagrangianTorusFibration.exists_fiberAction_eq`). It is packaged as an additive action
(`IsLagrangianTorusFibration.fiberAddAction`), so that Mathlib's orbit and stabilizer API applies.

The period lattice `Λ_b` (`IsLagrangianTorusFibration.periodLattice`) is the subgroup of the
covectors acting trivially on the fibre. Since the action is transitive and commutative, a covector
lies in `Λ_b` as soon as it fixes one point of the fibre
(`IsLagrangianTorusFibration.mem_periodLattice_iff_fiberAction_eq`,
`IsLagrangianTorusFibration.periodLattice_eq_stabilizer`), and two covectors act alike
on a point exactly when they differ by an element of `Λ_b`
(`IsLagrangianTorusFibration.fiberAction_eq_fiberAction_iff`). The period lattice is a discrete
subgroup (`IsLagrangianTorusFibration.discreteTopology_periodLattice`) spanning `T*_b B`
(`IsLagrangianTorusFibration.isZLattice_periodLattice`), hence a full lattice of rank `n`
(`IsLagrangianTorusFibration.finrank_periodLattice`), and the orbit map through any point of the
fibre descends to a homeomorphism `T*_b B / Λ_b ≃ₜ π⁻¹(b)`
(`IsLagrangianTorusFibration.quotientPeriodLatticeHomeomorph`).

The proofs transport the corresponding facts for the Hamiltonian flow action of coordinates
`κ ∘ π` near the fibre (`IsLagrangianTorusFibration.exists_coordinates`), in which the vector `v`
acts by the time-one flow of `v ⬝ᵥ (κ ∘ π)`
(`TauCeti.SmoothTwoForm.IsSymplectic.flowOf_hamiltonianVectorField_dotProduct`), that is, as the
covector `d(v ⬝ᵥ κ)_b`.

These fibrewise lattices are the fibres of the period lattice `Λ ⊆ T*B` of the fibration, whose
quotient `T*B / Λ` is the torus bundle associated with the fibration; that bundle is not constructed
here. Its model, for a lattice spanned by global closed one-forms, is
`TauCeti.CotangentBundle.LatticeQuotient`.

## Main definitions

* `IsLagrangianTorusFibration.hamiltonianFlowActionComp`: the Hamiltonian flow action of `ℝ^ι`
  generated by the components of `κ ∘ π`, for a smooth map `κ : B → ℝ^ι`.
* `IsLagrangianTorusFibration.fiberAction`: the action of `T*_b B` on the fibre over `b`.
* `IsLagrangianTorusFibration.fiberAddAction`: the same action, as an `AddAction`.
* `IsLagrangianTorusFibration.periodLattice`: the period lattice `Λ_b ⊆ T*_b B`.
* `IsLagrangianTorusFibration.quotientPeriodLatticeHomeomorph`: the homeomorphism
  `T*_b B / Λ_b ≃ₜ π⁻¹(b)` given by the orbit map through a point of the fibre.

## Main results

* `IsLagrangianTorusFibration.coe_fiberAction_eq_flowOf`: a covector `dg_b` acts by the time-one
  map of the Hamiltonian flow of `g ∘ π`.
* `IsLagrangianTorusFibration.fiberAction_add`, `IsLagrangianTorusFibration.exists_fiberAction_eq`:
  the action is an action of the additive group `T*_b B`, and it is transitive.
* `IsLagrangianTorusFibration.mem_periodLattice_iff_fiberAction_eq`,
  `IsLagrangianTorusFibration.mem_periodLattice_iff_flowOf_eq`: the period lattice is the
  stabilizer of any point of the fibre.
* `IsLagrangianTorusFibration.mem_periodLattice_iff_mem_hamiltonianFlowStabilizer`: for any smooth
  coordinates `κ` on `B`, the period lattice is the stabilizer of the Hamiltonian flow action of
  `κ ∘ π`, read through the covectors `d(v ⬝ᵥ κ)_b`.
* `IsLagrangianTorusFibration.discreteTopology_periodLattice`,
  `IsLagrangianTorusFibration.isZLattice_periodLattice`,
  `IsLagrangianTorusFibration.finrank_periodLattice`: the period lattice is a full lattice in
  `T*_b B`, of rank `dim B`. The first two are instances.

All in the namespace `TauCeti.SmoothTwoForm.IsNondegenerate`.

## References

* J. J. Duistermaat, *On global action-angle coordinates*, Comm. Pure Appl. Math. 33 (1980),
  687–706, Section 1 (the action of `T*B` on the fibres and the period lattice).
* A. Cannas da Silva, *Lectures on Symplectic Geometry*, Lecture Notes in Mathematics 1764,
  Springer, 2001, Section 18.
-/

public section

noncomputable section

open Function Set Module
open scoped ContDiff Manifold Topology

namespace TauCeti.SmoothTwoForm.IsNondegenerate.IsLagrangianTorusFibration

variable {E H M F H' B : Type*}
  [NormedAddCommGroup E] [NormedSpace ℝ E] [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] [TopologicalSpace H]
  {I : ModelWithCorners ℝ E H} [TopologicalSpace M] [ChartedSpace H M] [IsManifold I ∞ M]
  [T2Space M] [BoundarylessManifold I M] [I.Boundaryless]
  [NormedAddCommGroup F] [NormedSpace ℝ F] [FiniteDimensional ℝ F] [TopologicalSpace H']
  {J : ModelWithCorners ℝ F H'} [TopologicalSpace B] [ChartedSpace H' B] [IsManifold J ∞ B]
  [T2Space B]
  {σ : SmoothTwoForm I M} {hσ : σ.IsNondegenerate} {π : M → B}

variable (h : hσ.IsLagrangianTorusFibration J π) (hσc : σ.IsClosed)

/-! ### The Hamiltonian flow action of functions on the base -/

section FlowAction

variable {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι] {κ : B → ι → ℝ}

omit [T2Space M] [BoundarylessManifold I M] [I.Boundaryless] [FiniteDimensional ℝ F]
  [IsManifold J ∞ B] [T2Space B] in
include h in
/-- **Pulled-back functions Poisson-commute everywhere.** For `κ : B → ℝ^ι` differentiable on the
base, the components of `κ ∘ π` Poisson-commute at every point of `M`. -/
theorem poissonBracket_comp_apply_eq_zero_of_mdifferentiable
    (hκ : MDifferentiable J 𝓘(ℝ, ι → ℝ) κ) (i j : ι) (y : M) :
    σ.poissonBracket ((κ ∘ π) · i) ((κ ∘ π) · j) y = 0 :=
  h.poissonBracket_comp_apply_eq_zero (hκ (π y)) i j

omit [I.Boundaryless] [FiniteDimensional ℝ F] [T2Space B] in
include h in
/-- The components of `κ ∘ π` have complete Hamiltonian vector fields, for a `C²` map
`κ : B → ℝ^ι`: their integral curves stay in the compact fibres of `π`. -/
theorem isCompleteVectorField_hamiltonianVectorField_comp_apply
    (hκ : ContMDiff J 𝓘(ℝ, ι → ℝ) 2 κ) (i : ι) :
    IsCompleteVectorField (σ.hamiltonianVectorField ((κ ∘ π) · i)) :=
  h.isCompleteVectorField_hamiltonianVectorField_comp (g := fun b ↦ κ b i) h.isProperMap
    (contMDiff_pi_module_iff.1 hκ i)

/-- **The Hamiltonian flow action of functions on the base.** For a smooth map `κ : B → ℝ^ι`, the
vector `v ∈ ℝ^ι` acts on `M` by the time-one map of the Hamiltonian flow of `v ⬝ᵥ (κ ∘ π)`
(`hamiltonianFlowActionComp_apply`). The components of `κ ∘ π` Poisson-commute and have complete
Hamiltonian vector fields, so this is `TauCeti.SmoothTwoForm.IsSymplectic.hamiltonianFlowAction`
for them. -/
def hamiltonianFlowActionComp (hκ : ContMDiff J 𝓘(ℝ, ι → ℝ) ∞ κ) (v : ι → ℝ) : M → M :=
  ((⟨hσc, hσ⟩ : σ.IsSymplectic).hamiltonianFlowAction (hκ.comp h.contMDiff)
    (h.poissonBracket_comp_apply_eq_zero_of_mdifferentiable (hκ.mdifferentiable (by simp)))
    (h.isCompleteVectorField_hamiltonianVectorField_comp_apply (hκ.of_le (by simp))) v).toMul

omit [FiniteDimensional ℝ F] [T2Space B] in
/-- The vector `v` acts by the time-one map of the Hamiltonian flow of `v ⬝ᵥ (κ ∘ π)`. -/
theorem hamiltonianFlowActionComp_apply (hκ : ContMDiff J 𝓘(ℝ, ι → ℝ) ∞ κ) (v : ι → ℝ) (x : M) :
    h.hamiltonianFlowActionComp hσc hκ v x =
      flowOf (σ.hamiltonianVectorField fun y ↦ v ⬝ᵥ (κ ∘ π) y) 1 x := by
  rw [(⟨hσc, hσ⟩ : σ.IsSymplectic).flowOf_hamiltonianVectorField_dotProduct, one_smul,
    hamiltonianFlowActionComp]

omit [FiniteDimensional ℝ F] [T2Space B] in
/-- The zero vector acts as the identity. -/
@[simp]
theorem hamiltonianFlowActionComp_zero (hκ : ContMDiff J 𝓘(ℝ, ι → ℝ) ∞ κ) (x : M) :
    h.hamiltonianFlowActionComp hσc hκ 0 x = x :=
  (⟨hσc, hσ⟩ : σ.IsSymplectic).hamiltonianFlowAction_zero_apply _ _ _ x

omit [FiniteDimensional ℝ F] [T2Space B] in
/-- The action of `v + w` is the action of `v` after that of `w`. -/
theorem hamiltonianFlowActionComp_add (hκ : ContMDiff J 𝓘(ℝ, ι → ℝ) ∞ κ) (v w : ι → ℝ) (x : M) :
    h.hamiltonianFlowActionComp hσc hκ (v + w) x =
      h.hamiltonianFlowActionComp hσc hκ v (h.hamiltonianFlowActionComp hσc hκ w x) :=
  (⟨hσc, hσ⟩ : σ.IsSymplectic).hamiltonianFlowAction_add_apply _ _ _ v w x

omit [FiniteDimensional ℝ F] [T2Space B] in
/-- Two vectors act alike on `x` exactly when their difference fixes `x`. -/
theorem hamiltonianFlowActionComp_apply_eq_iff (hκ : ContMDiff J 𝓘(ℝ, ι → ℝ) ∞ κ)
    {v w : ι → ℝ} {x : M} :
    h.hamiltonianFlowActionComp hσc hκ v x = h.hamiltonianFlowActionComp hσc hκ w x ↔
      h.hamiltonianFlowActionComp hσc hκ (-v + w) x = x :=
  ((⟨hσc, hσ⟩ : σ.IsSymplectic).hamiltonianFlowAction_apply_eq_iff _ _ _).trans
    (IsSymplectic.mem_hamiltonianFlowStabilizer _ _ _ _)

omit [FiniteDimensional ℝ F] [T2Space B] in
/-- The Hamiltonian flow action of `κ ∘ π` is smooth jointly in the vector and the point. -/
theorem contMDiff_hamiltonianFlowActionComp_uncurry (hκ : ContMDiff J 𝓘(ℝ, ι → ℝ) ∞ κ) :
    ContMDiff (𝓘(ℝ, ι → ℝ).prod I) I ∞
      fun p : (ι → ℝ) × M ↦ h.hamiltonianFlowActionComp hσc hκ p.1 p.2 :=
  (⟨hσc, hσ⟩ : σ.IsSymplectic).contMDiff_hamiltonianFlowAction_uncurry _ _ _

omit [FiniteDimensional ℝ F] [T2Space B] in
/-- **Moving a map by the Hamiltonian flow action of `κ ∘ π`.** For maps `f : N → ℝ^ι` and
`g : N → M`, differentiable at `n`, the map `n ↦ f n • g n` pulls `σ` back to
`g^* σ + ∑ᵢ dfᵢ ∧ d(κᵢ ∘ π ∘ g)` at `n`. This is
`TauCeti.SmoothTwoForm.IsSymplectic.eval₂_mfderiv_hamiltonianFlowAction_comp` for the components
of `κ ∘ π`. -/
theorem eval₂_mfderiv_hamiltonianFlowActionComp_comp {E'' H'' N : Type*}
    [NormedAddCommGroup E''] [NormedSpace ℝ E''] [TopologicalSpace H'']
    {I' : ModelWithCorners ℝ E'' H''} [TopologicalSpace N] [ChartedSpace H'' N]
    (hκ : ContMDiff J 𝓘(ℝ, ι → ℝ) ∞ κ) {f : N → ι → ℝ} {g : N → M} {n : N}
    (hf : MDifferentiableAt I' 𝓘(ℝ, ι → ℝ) f n) (hg : MDifferentiableAt I' I g n)
    (ξ ξ' : TangentSpace I' n) :
    SmoothBundleForm.eval₂ σ (h.hamiltonianFlowActionComp hσc hκ (f n) (g n))
        (mfderiv I' I (fun n ↦ h.hamiltonianFlowActionComp hσc hκ (f n) (g n)) n ξ)
        (mfderiv I' I (fun n ↦ h.hamiltonianFlowActionComp hσc hκ (f n) (g n)) n ξ') =
      SmoothBundleForm.eval₂ σ (g n) (mfderiv I' I g n ξ) (mfderiv I' I g n ξ') +
        (mfderiv I' 𝓘(ℝ, ι → ℝ) f n ξ ⬝ᵥ mfderiv I' 𝓘(ℝ, ι → ℝ) ((κ ∘ π) ∘ g) n ξ' -
          mfderiv I' 𝓘(ℝ, ι → ℝ) f n ξ' ⬝ᵥ mfderiv I' 𝓘(ℝ, ι → ℝ) ((κ ∘ π) ∘ g) n ξ) :=
  (⟨hσc, hσ⟩ : σ.IsSymplectic).eval₂_mfderiv_hamiltonianFlowAction_comp _ _ _ hf hg ξ ξ'

end FlowAction

variable (b : B)

/-! ### Coordinates around a fibre and their Hamiltonian flow action -/

/-- The coordinates around the fibre over `b` chosen by `exists_coordinates`. -/
private def coord : B → Fin (finrank ℝ F) → ℝ :=
  (h.exists_coordinates b).choose

/-- The differential at `b` of the coordinates `coord`. -/
private def coordEquiv : F ≃L[ℝ] (Fin (finrank ℝ F) → ℝ) :=
  (h.exists_coordinates b).choose_spec.choose

omit [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] [T2Space M] [BoundarylessManifold I M] [I.Boundaryless] in
private theorem coord_spec :
    ContMDiff J 𝓘(ℝ, Fin (finrank ℝ F) → ℝ) ∞ (h.coord b) ∧
      mfderiv J 𝓘(ℝ, Fin (finrank ℝ F) → ℝ) (h.coord b) b =
        (h.coordEquiv b : F →L[ℝ] Fin (finrank ℝ F) → ℝ) ∧
      (∀ y ∈ π ⁻¹' {b}, IsRegularPoint I 𝓘(ℝ, Fin (finrank ℝ F) → ℝ) (h.coord b ∘ π) y) ∧
      ∀ x ∈ π ⁻¹' {b},
        connectedComponentIn ((h.coord b ∘ π) ⁻¹' {h.coord b (π x)}) x = π ⁻¹' {b} :=
  (h.exists_coordinates b).choose_spec.choose_spec

omit [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] [T2Space M] [BoundarylessManifold I M] [I.Boundaryless] in
/-- The fibre over `b` is the connected component of each of its points in its level of the
coordinates `coord ∘ π`. -/
private theorem connectedComponentIn_coord_comp (x : π ⁻¹' {b}) :
    connectedComponentIn ((h.coord b ∘ π) ⁻¹' {(h.coord b ∘ π) x}) x = π ⁻¹' {b} :=
  (h.coord_spec b).2.2.2 x x.property

omit [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] [T2Space M] [BoundarylessManifold I M] [I.Boundaryless] in
/-- The coordinates `coord ∘ π` are regular along the fibre over `b`. -/
private theorem isRegularPoint_coord_comp {y : M} (hy : y ∈ π ⁻¹' {b}) :
    IsRegularPoint I 𝓘(ℝ, Fin (finrank ℝ F) → ℝ) (h.coord b ∘ π) y :=
  (h.coord_spec b).2.2.1 y hy

omit [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] [T2Space M] [BoundarylessManifold I M] [I.Boundaryless] in
/-- The coordinates `coord ∘ π` are regular on the connected component of a point of the fibre
in its level. -/
private theorem isRegularPoint_coord_comp_of_mem_connectedComponentIn (x : π ⁻¹' {b}) :
    ∀ y ∈ connectedComponentIn ((h.coord b ∘ π) ⁻¹' {(h.coord b ∘ π) x}) x,
      IsRegularPoint I 𝓘(ℝ, Fin (finrank ℝ F) → ℝ) (h.coord b ∘ π) y := fun _ hy ↦
  h.isRegularPoint_coord_comp b ((h.connectedComponentIn_coord_comp b x).subset hy)

omit [T2Space M] [BoundarylessManifold I M] [I.Boundaryless] [FiniteDimensional ℝ F]
  [IsManifold J ∞ B] [T2Space B] in
include h in
/-- The number of coordinates is half the dimension of `M`. -/
private theorem two_mul_card_eq (x : M) :
    2 * Fintype.card (Fin (finrank ℝ F)) = finrank ℝ E :=
  have : Nonempty M := ⟨x⟩
  h.two_mul_card_fin_finrank

omit [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] [T2Space M] [BoundarylessManifold I M] [I.Boundaryless] in
private theorem contMDiff_coord_comp :
    ContMDiff I 𝓘(ℝ, Fin (finrank ℝ F) → ℝ) ∞ (h.coord b ∘ π) :=
  (h.coord_spec b).1.comp h.contMDiff

omit [T2Space M] [BoundarylessManifold I M] [I.Boundaryless] in
private theorem poissonBracket_coord_comp (i j : Fin (finrank ℝ F)) (y : M) :
    σ.poissonBracket ((h.coord b ∘ π) · i) ((h.coord b ∘ π) · j) y = 0 :=
  h.poissonBracket_comp_apply_eq_zero_of_mdifferentiable
    ((h.coord_spec b).1.mdifferentiable (by simp)) i j y

omit [I.Boundaryless] in
private theorem isCompleteVectorField_coord_comp (i : Fin (finrank ℝ F)) :
    IsCompleteVectorField (σ.hamiltonianVectorField ((h.coord b ∘ π) · i)) :=
  h.isCompleteVectorField_hamiltonianVectorField_comp_apply ((h.coord_spec b).1.of_le (by simp)) i

/-- The stabilizer of `x` for the Hamiltonian flow action of the coordinates `coord ∘ π`. -/
private abbrev coordStabilizer (x : M) : AddSubgroup (Fin (finrank ℝ F) → ℝ) :=
  (⟨hσc, hσ⟩ : σ.IsSymplectic).hamiltonianFlowStabilizer (h.contMDiff_coord_comp b)
    (h.poissonBracket_coord_comp b)
    (h.isCompleteVectorField_coord_comp b)
    x

/-- The coordinates of a covector at `b` in the basis dual to the coordinates `coord`. -/
private def dualCoord : (F →L[ℝ] ℝ) ≃L[ℝ] (Fin (finrank ℝ F) → ℝ) :=
  (((h.coordEquiv b).arrowCongr (ContinuousLinearEquiv.refl ℝ ℝ)).toLinearEquiv.trans
    (LinearMap.toContinuousLinearMap.symm.trans
      (dotProductEquiv ℝ (Fin (finrank ℝ F))).symm)).toContinuousLinearEquiv

omit [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] [T2Space M] [BoundarylessManifold I M] [I.Boundaryless] in
private theorem dualCoord_apply (α : F →L[ℝ] ℝ) (i : Fin (finrank ℝ F)) :
    h.dualCoord b α i = α ((h.coordEquiv b).symm (Pi.single i 1)) := by
  simp [dualCoord, dotProductEquiv]

/-! ### The action of the cotangent space on a fibre -/

/-- **The action of `T*_b B` on the fibre over `b`.** A covector `α` acts on the fibre `π⁻¹(b)` by
the time-one map of the Hamiltonian flow of `g ∘ π`, for any `C²` function `g` on `B` with
`dg_b = α` (`coe_fiberAction_eq_flowOf`). -/
def fiberAction (α : F →L[ℝ] ℝ) (x : π ⁻¹' {b}) : π ⁻¹' {b} :=
  ⟨h.hamiltonianFlowActionComp hσc (h.coord_spec b).1 (h.dualCoord b α) x,
    (h.connectedComponentIn_coord_comp b x).subset <|
    (⟨hσc, hσ⟩ : σ.IsSymplectic).hamiltonianFlowAction_apply_mem_connectedComponentIn _ _ _ x _⟩

private theorem coe_fiberAction (α : F →L[ℝ] ℝ) (x : π ⁻¹' {b}) :
    (h.fiberAction hσc b α x : M) =
      h.hamiltonianFlowActionComp hσc (h.coord_spec b).1 (h.dualCoord b α) x :=
  (rfl)

omit [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] [T2Space M] [BoundarylessManifold I M] [I.Boundaryless] in
/-- A covector `α` at `b` is the differential at `b` of the function `v ⬝ᵥ coord`, where `v` are the
dual coordinates of `α`. -/
private theorem mvfderiv_dualCoord_dotProduct_coord (α : F →L[ℝ] ℝ) :
    mvfderiv J (fun c ↦ h.dualCoord b α ⬝ᵥ h.coord b c) b = α := by
  classical
  let φ : (Fin (finrank ℝ F) → ℝ) →L[ℝ] ℝ := LinearMap.toContinuousLinearMap
    (dotProductEquiv ℝ (Fin (finrank ℝ F)) (h.dualCoord b α))
  have h2 : φ.comp (h.coordEquiv b : F →L[ℝ] Fin (finrank ℝ F) → ℝ) = α :=
    (h.dualCoord b).injective (funext fun i ↦ by simp [φ, dualCoord_apply])
  -- The chain rule for the linear map `φ`, with `d(coord)_b = coordEquiv`.
  refine ContinuousLinearMap.ext fun w ↦
    (φ.mvfderiv_comp_apply (((h.coord_spec b).1 b).mdifferentiableAt (by simp)) w).trans ?_
  rw [mvfderiv_apply_eq_mfderiv_apply, (h.coord_spec b).2.1]
  exact (φ.comp_apply _ w).symm.trans (DFunLike.congr_fun h2 w)

/-- **A covector `dg_b` acts by the time-one map of the Hamiltonian flow of `g ∘ π`.** For every
`C²` function `g` on `B` with differential `α` at `b`, the action of `α` moves each point `x` of
the fibre over `b` to the time-one image of `x` under the flow of the Hamiltonian vector field of
`g ∘ π`. -/
theorem coe_fiberAction_eq_flowOf {α : F →L[ℝ] ℝ} {g : B → ℝ}
    (hg : ContMDiff J 𝓘(ℝ) 2 g) (hgα : mvfderiv J g b = α) (x : π ⁻¹' {b}) :
    (h.fiberAction hσc b α x : M) = flowOf (σ.hamiltonianVectorField (g ∘ π)) 1 x := by
  classical
  -- The covector `α` is the differential at `b` of the function `v ⬝ᵥ coord`, where `v` are the
  -- dual coordinates of `α`.
  let φ : (Fin (finrank ℝ F) → ℝ) →L[ℝ] ℝ := LinearMap.toContinuousLinearMap
    (dotProductEquiv ℝ (Fin (finrank ℝ F)) (h.dualCoord b α))
  have hφ : ContMDiff J 𝓘(ℝ) 2 (φ ∘ h.coord b) :=
    (φ.contMDiff.comp (h.coord_spec b).1).of_le (by simp)
  have hdφ : mvfderiv J (φ ∘ h.coord b) b = α := h.mvfderiv_dualCoord_dotProduct_coord b α
  have hx : π x = b := x.property
  rw [coe_fiberAction, hamiltonianFlowActionComp_apply]
  exact h.flowOf_hamiltonianVectorField_comp_eq h.isProperMap hφ hg
    (by rw [hx, hdφ, hgα]) 1

/-- The zero covector acts as the identity on the fibre. -/
@[simp]
theorem fiberAction_zero (x : π ⁻¹' {b}) : h.fiberAction hσc b 0 x = x :=
  Subtype.ext <| by
    rw [coe_fiberAction, map_zero, hamiltonianFlowActionComp_zero]

/-- **The action of `T*_b B` on the fibre is additive**: `α + β` acts as `α` after `β`. -/
theorem fiberAction_add (α β : F →L[ℝ] ℝ) (x : π ⁻¹' {b}) :
    h.fiberAction hσc b (α + β) x = h.fiberAction hσc b α (h.fiberAction hσc b β x) :=
  Subtype.ext <| by
    rw [coe_fiberAction, coe_fiberAction, coe_fiberAction, map_add, hamiltonianFlowActionComp_add]

/-- The actions of two covectors on the fibre commute. -/
theorem fiberAction_comm (α β : F →L[ℝ] ℝ) (x : π ⁻¹' {b}) :
    h.fiberAction hσc b α (h.fiberAction hσc b β x) =
      h.fiberAction hσc b β (h.fiberAction hσc b α x) := by
  rw [← fiberAction_add, add_comm, fiberAction_add]

/-- **The action of `T*_b B` on the fibre over `b` is transitive.** -/
theorem exists_fiberAction_eq (x y : π ⁻¹' {b}) : ∃ α, h.fiberAction hσc b α x = y := by
  obtain ⟨v, hv⟩ := (⟨hσc, hσ⟩ : σ.IsSymplectic).exists_hamiltonianFlowAction_apply_eq
    (h.contMDiff_coord_comp b)
    (h.poissonBracket_coord_comp b)
    (h.isCompleteVectorField_coord_comp b)
    (h.two_mul_card_eq x)
    (h.isRegularPoint_coord_comp_of_mem_connectedComponentIn b x)
    ((h.connectedComponentIn_coord_comp b x).symm.subset y.property)
  refine ⟨(h.dualCoord b).symm v, Subtype.ext ?_⟩
  rw [coe_fiberAction, ContinuousLinearEquiv.apply_symm_apply]
  exact hv

/-- **The action of `T*_b B` on the fibre over `b` as an additive action.** The covector `α` acts
on `x` by `α +ᵥ x = fiberAction α x`. It depends on the hypotheses on `σ` and `π`, so it is not an
instance; it makes Mathlib's orbit and stabilizer API available for this action. -/
abbrev fiberAddAction : AddAction (F →L[ℝ] ℝ) (π ⁻¹' {b}) where
  vadd := h.fiberAction hσc b
  zero_vadd := h.fiberAction_zero hσc b
  add_vadd := h.fiberAction_add hσc b

/-- The covector `α` acts on `x` for `fiberAddAction` by `fiberAction α x`. -/
@[simp]
theorem fiberAddAction_vadd (α : F →L[ℝ] ℝ) (x : π ⁻¹' {b}) :
    (letI := h.fiberAddAction hσc b; α +ᵥ x) = h.fiberAction hσc b α x :=
  rfl

/-- The additive action of `T*_b B` on the fibre over `b` is transitive. -/
theorem isPretransitive_fiberAddAction :
    letI := h.fiberAddAction hσc b
    AddAction.IsPretransitive (F →L[ℝ] ℝ) (π ⁻¹' {b}) :=
  letI := h.fiberAddAction hσc b
  ⟨h.exists_fiberAction_eq hσc b⟩

/-! ### The period lattice -/

/-- **The period lattice** `Λ_b ⊆ T*_b B` of the fibration at `b`: the subgroup of the covectors
acting trivially on the fibre over `b`, that is, the intersection of the stabilizers of the points
of the fibre. It is the stabilizer of any single point of the fibre (`periodLattice_eq_stabilizer`),
and it is a full lattice in `T*_b B` (`isZLattice_periodLattice`). -/
def periodLattice : AddSubgroup (F →L[ℝ] ℝ) :=
  letI := h.fiberAddAction hσc b
  ⨅ x : π ⁻¹' {b}, AddAction.stabilizer (F →L[ℝ] ℝ) x

/-- A covector lies in the period lattice exactly when it fixes every point of the fibre. -/
@[simp]
theorem mem_periodLattice {α : F →L[ℝ] ℝ} :
    α ∈ h.periodLattice hσc b ↔ ∀ x, h.fiberAction hσc b α x = x :=
  letI := h.fiberAddAction hσc b
  AddSubgroup.mem_iInf.trans (forall_congr' fun _ ↦ AddAction.mem_stabilizer_iff)

/-- **The period lattice is the stabilizer of any point of the fibre.** A covector acts trivially
on the fibre as soon as it fixes one of its points, since the action is transitive and
commutative. -/
theorem mem_periodLattice_iff_fiberAction_eq {α : F →L[ℝ] ℝ} (x : π ⁻¹' {b}) :
    α ∈ h.periodLattice hσc b ↔ h.fiberAction hσc b α x = x := by
  refine (h.mem_periodLattice hσc b).trans ⟨fun hα ↦ hα x, fun hα y ↦ ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨β, rfl⟩ := h.exists_fiberAction_eq hσc b x y
  rw [fiberAction_comm, hα]

/-- **The period lattice is the stabilizer of any point of the fibre**, for the additive action
`fiberAddAction`. -/
theorem periodLattice_eq_stabilizer (x : π ⁻¹' {b}) :
    h.periodLattice hσc b = (letI := h.fiberAddAction hσc b; AddAction.stabilizer _ x) :=
  letI := h.fiberAddAction hσc b
  AddSubgroup.ext fun α ↦ (h.mem_periodLattice_iff_fiberAction_eq hσc b x).trans
    ((AddAction.mem_stabilizer_iff (a := x) (g := α)).trans (by rw [fiberAddAction_vadd])).symm

/-- **The period lattice in terms of Hamiltonian flows.** The differential `α` at `b` of a `C²`
function `g` on `B` lies in the period lattice exactly when the time-one map of the Hamiltonian
flow of `g ∘ π` fixes some, equivalently every, point of the fibre over `b`. -/
theorem mem_periodLattice_iff_flowOf_eq {α : F →L[ℝ] ℝ} {g : B → ℝ} (hg : ContMDiff J 𝓘(ℝ) 2 g)
    (hgα : mvfderiv J g b = α) (x : π ⁻¹' {b}) :
    α ∈ h.periodLattice hσc b ↔ flowOf (σ.hamiltonianVectorField (g ∘ π)) 1 x = x := by
  rw [h.mem_periodLattice_iff_fiberAction_eq hσc b x, Subtype.ext_iff,
    h.coe_fiberAction_eq_flowOf hσc b hg hgα]

/-- **The period lattice in terms of the Hamiltonian flow action of coordinates.** Let
`κ : B → ℝ^ι` be smooth, so that the components of `κ ∘ π` are Poisson-commuting functions with
complete Hamiltonian vector fields, and let `x` be a point of the fibre over `b`. Then the covector
`α = d(v ⬝ᵥ κ)_b` lies in the period lattice at `b` exactly when `v` lies in the stabilizer of `x`
for the Hamiltonian flow action of `κ ∘ π`. -/
theorem mem_periodLattice_iff_mem_hamiltonianFlowStabilizer {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι]
    {κ : B → ι → ℝ} (hκ : ContMDiff J 𝓘(ℝ, ι → ℝ) ∞ κ)
    (hcomm : ∀ i j y, σ.poissonBracket ((κ ∘ π) · i) ((κ ∘ π) · j) y = 0)
    (hc : ∀ i, IsCompleteVectorField (σ.hamiltonianVectorField ((κ ∘ π) · i)))
    (x : π ⁻¹' {b}) (v : ι → ℝ) {α : F →L[ℝ] ℝ} (hα : mvfderiv J (fun c ↦ v ⬝ᵥ κ c) b = α) :
    α ∈ h.periodLattice hσc b ↔
      v ∈ (⟨hσc, hσ⟩ : σ.IsSymplectic).hamiltonianFlowStabilizer (hκ.comp h.contMDiff) hcomm hc x
    := by
  classical
  have hg : ContMDiff J 𝓘(ℝ) 2 fun c ↦ v ⬝ᵥ κ c :=
    ((LinearMap.toContinuousLinearMap (dotProductEquiv ℝ ι v)).contMDiff.comp hκ).of_le
      (by simp)
  rw [h.mem_periodLattice_iff_flowOf_eq hσc b hg hα x,
    IsSymplectic.mem_hamiltonianFlowStabilizer]
  -- The time-one map of the flow of `v ⬝ᵥ (κ ∘ π)` is the action of `v`.
  have hflow := (⟨hσc, hσ⟩ : σ.IsSymplectic).flowOf_hamiltonianVectorField_dotProduct
    (hκ.comp h.contMDiff) hcomm hc v 1 x
  rw [one_smul] at hflow
  exact iff_of_eq (congrArg (· = (x : M)) hflow)

/-- The period lattice is the stabilizer of the coordinate flow action, read in dual coordinates. -/
private theorem mem_periodLattice_iff_mem_coordStabilizer {α : F →L[ℝ] ℝ}
    (x : π ⁻¹' {b}) :
    α ∈ h.periodLattice hσc b ↔ h.dualCoord b α ∈ h.coordStabilizer hσc b x :=
  h.mem_periodLattice_iff_mem_hamiltonianFlowStabilizer hσc b (h.coord_spec b).1
    (h.poissonBracket_coord_comp b) (h.isCompleteVectorField_coord_comp b) x _
    (h.mvfderiv_dualCoord_dotProduct_coord b α)

/-- Two covectors act alike on a point of the fibre exactly when they differ by an element of the
period lattice. -/
theorem fiberAction_eq_fiberAction_iff {α β : F →L[ℝ] ℝ} (x : π ⁻¹' {b}) :
    h.fiberAction hσc b α x = h.fiberAction hσc b β x ↔ -α + β ∈ h.periodLattice hσc b := by
  rw [Subtype.ext_iff, coe_fiberAction, coe_fiberAction, hamiltonianFlowActionComp_apply_eq_iff,
    ← map_neg, ← map_add, ← coe_fiberAction, ← Subtype.ext_iff,
    h.mem_periodLattice_iff_fiberAction_eq hσc b x]

/-- The dual coordinates map the period lattice onto the stabilizer of a point of the fibre for the
coordinate flow action. -/
private theorem map_dualCoord_periodLattice (x : π ⁻¹' {b}) :
    (h.periodLattice hσc b).map (h.dualCoord b).toContinuousAddEquiv.toAddEquiv.toAddMonoidHom =
      h.coordStabilizer hσc b x := by
  ext v
  rw [AddSubgroup.mem_map_equiv, h.mem_periodLattice_iff_mem_coordStabilizer hσc b x]
  exact iff_of_eq (congrArg (· ∈ _) ((h.dualCoord b).apply_symm_apply v))

/-- The stabilizer of a point of the fibre for the coordinate flow action is discrete. -/
private theorem discreteTopology_coordStabilizer (x : π ⁻¹' {b}) :
    DiscreteTopology (h.coordStabilizer hσc b x) :=
  (⟨hσc, hσ⟩ : σ.IsSymplectic).discreteTopology_hamiltonianFlowStabilizer
    (h.contMDiff_coord_comp b)
    (h.poissonBracket_coord_comp b)
    (h.isCompleteVectorField_coord_comp b)
    (h.isRegularPoint_coord_comp b x.property)

/-- **The period lattice is discrete.** -/
instance discreteTopology_periodLattice : DiscreteTopology (h.periodLattice hσc b) := by
  obtain ⟨x⟩ := (h.isConnected_preimage_singleton b).nonempty.to_subtype
  have := h.discreteTopology_coordStabilizer hσc b x
  -- The dual coordinates embed the period lattice into the discrete stabilizer of `x`.
  exact DiscreteTopology.of_continuous_injective
    (f := fun α : h.periodLattice hσc b ↦ (⟨h.dualCoord b α,
      (h.mem_periodLattice_iff_mem_coordStabilizer hσc b x).1 α.property⟩ : h.coordStabilizer hσc b
          x))
    (((h.dualCoord b).continuous.comp continuous_subtypeVal).subtype_mk _)
    fun _ _ hαβ ↦ Subtype.ext ((h.dualCoord b).injective (congrArg Subtype.val hαβ))

/-- **The period lattice is a full lattice.** The period lattice spans `T*_b B`, so with its
discreteness (`discreteTopology_periodLattice`) it is a `ℤ`-lattice in `T*_b B`. Hence the fibre
over `b`, which is homeomorphic to `T*_b B / Λ_b` (`quotientPeriodLatticeHomeomorph`), is a torus of
dimension `dim B`. -/
instance isZLattice_periodLattice : IsZLattice ℝ (h.periodLattice hσc b).toIntSubmodule := by
  obtain ⟨x⟩ := (h.isConnected_preimage_singleton b).nonempty.to_subtype
  have := h.discreteTopology_coordStabilizer hσc b x
  have : IsZLattice ℝ (h.coordStabilizer hσc b x).toIntSubmodule :=
    (⟨hσc, hσ⟩ : σ.IsSymplectic).isZLattice_hamiltonianFlowStabilizer
      (h.contMDiff_coord_comp b)
      (h.poissonBracket_coord_comp b)
      (h.isCompleteVectorField_coord_comp b)
      (h.two_mul_card_eq x)
      (h.isRegularPoint_coord_comp_of_mem_connectedComponentIn b x)
      (by rw [h.connectedComponentIn_coord_comp b x]; exact h.isCompact_preimage_singleton b)
  -- The period lattice is the preimage of the stabilizer of `x` under the dual coordinates.
  have hcomap : (h.periodLattice hσc b).toIntSubmodule =
      ZLattice.comap ℝ (h.coordStabilizer hσc b x).toIntSubmodule (h.dualCoord b).toLinearMap :=
    Submodule.ext fun _ ↦ h.mem_periodLattice_iff_mem_coordStabilizer hσc b x
  refine ⟨?_⟩
  rw [hcomap]
  exact IsZLattice.span_top

/-- **The period lattice has rank `dim B`.** -/
theorem finrank_periodLattice :
    finrank ℤ (h.periodLattice hσc b).toIntSubmodule = finrank ℝ F := by
  rw [ZLattice.rank ℝ, (h.dualCoord b).toLinearEquiv.finrank_eq, finrank_fin_fun]

/-! ### The fibre as the torus `T*_b B / Λ_b` -/

/-- **The fibre over `b` is the torus `T*_b B / Λ_b`.** For a point `x` of the fibre, the orbit
map `α ↦ fiberAction α x` of the action of `T*_b B` descends to a homeomorphism from the quotient of
`T*_b B` by the period lattice onto the fibre over `b`. It is the quotient of the dual coordinates,
followed by the identification of the quotient of `ℝⁿ` by the stabilizer of `x` for the coordinate
flow action with the connected component of `x` in its level, which is the fibre. -/
def quotientPeriodLatticeHomeomorph (x : π ⁻¹' {b}) :
    (F →L[ℝ] ℝ) ⧸ h.periodLattice hσc b ≃ₜ π ⁻¹' {b} :=
  (Homeomorph.ofClass ((h.dualCoord b).toContinuousAddEquiv.quotientCongr _ _
      (h.map_dualCoord_periodLattice hσc b x))).trans <|
    ((⟨hσc, hσ⟩ : σ.IsSymplectic).quotientHamiltonianFlowStabilizerHomeomorph
      (h.contMDiff_coord_comp b)
      (h.poissonBracket_coord_comp b)
      (h.isCompleteVectorField_coord_comp b)
      (h.two_mul_card_eq x)
      (h.isRegularPoint_coord_comp_of_mem_connectedComponentIn b x)).trans <|
    Homeomorph.setCongr (h.connectedComponentIn_coord_comp b x)

/-- The homeomorphism `T*_b B / Λ_b ≃ₜ π⁻¹(b)` sends the class of `α` to `fiberAction α x`. -/
@[simp]
theorem quotientPeriodLatticeHomeomorph_mk (x : π ⁻¹' {b}) (α : F →L[ℝ] ℝ) :
    h.quotientPeriodLatticeHomeomorph hσc b x α = h.fiberAction hσc b α x :=
  Subtype.ext <| by
    rw [quotientPeriodLatticeHomeomorph, Homeomorph.trans_apply, Homeomorph.trans_apply,
      Homeomorph.coe_ofClass, ContinuousAddEquiv.quotientCongr_mk,
      ContinuousLinearEquiv.toContinuousAddEquiv_coe, coe_fiberAction, hamiltonianFlowActionComp]
    -- `Homeomorph.setCongr` does not change the underlying point.
    exact IsSymplectic.coe_quotientHamiltonianFlowStabilizerHomeomorph_mk _ _ _ _ _ _ _

end TauCeti.SmoothTwoForm.IsNondegenerate.IsLagrangianTorusFibration
